<BaseLayout title="AWD warning and diagnosis">
  <h1>AWD warning and diagnosis</h1>
  <p>This guide helps preserve useful evidence when an AWD warning or driveline symptom occurs. It is not a repair procedure and does not identify a failed component.</p>

  <div class="note"><strong>Warning:</strong> If the driver display says to stop, or the vehicle has abnormal braking, steering, severe vibration, smoke, or a major fluid leak, stop in a safe place and arrange assistance. Do not continue testing a vehicle that may be unsafe.</div>

  <h2>AWD disabled message</h2>
  <p>Volvo's AWD system information describes an “AWD disabled” / service-required message as an indication that an electrical fault has occurred in the AWD system. Volvo directs the driver to have the system checked by a trained and qualified technician.</p>

  <h2>Capture this information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Photograph the complete driver-display message and warning symbol.</li>
    <li>Record the odometer, outside temperature, and whether the vehicle was started cold or was already warm.</li>
    <li>Note whether the message appeared during startup, acceleration, turning, parking maneuvers, or steady-speed driving.</li>
    <li>Record any recent battery work, tire replacement, collision, underbody impact, or drivetrain repair.</li>
    <li>Describe noises, vibration, binding, wheelspin, or changes in traction without deliberately reproducing a fault.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Diagnostic approach</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Save a complete vehicle scan before clearing codes or disconnecting the battery.</li>
    <li>Record the reporting module, full fault identifier, status, occurrence count, and any available freeze-frame data.</li>
    <li>Check for related low-voltage or communication faults; do not assume an AWD mechanical component has failed.</li>
    <li>Have a Volvo-capable technician follow the VIN-specific diagnostic tree and inspect the relevant wiring, connectors, and driveline components.</li>
    <li>Verify the repair with a complete scan and the prescribed post-repair checks.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Do not do this</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not replace the rear drive unit, coupling, angle gear, or propeller shaft based only on the dashboard message.</li>
    <li>Do not mix or substitute drivetrain fluids based on a generic Volvo specification.</li>
    <li>Do not run the vehicle on a lift or perform wheel-speed tests without the correct professional procedure and equipment.</li>
    <li>Do not erase codes before recording them.</li>
  </ul>

